i dropped some eggs he like accidentally  made the cut stranger things is one of  the biggest tv hits  of all time due in large part to its  amazing cast  along with being incredible actors it  turns out that they're also some  seriously  impressive improvisers even though the  show's scripted  some of the most impactful moments from  all three seasons were actually  improv like some hilariously awkward  unscripted moments that even  the most professional actors couldn't  keep a straight face for  it was not written in the script because  it was not written  one of the most infamous unscripted  moments in stranger things history was  the kiss between max and lucas  in season two well the actress behind  max  sadie sink who was only 15 at the time  and had never been kissed  was not told about the big moment before  arriving on set  but when ross duffer joked about it and  she freaked out and became extremely  uncomfortable  he decided that he just had to add it in  just to mess with her  he said in an interview that it was her  fault that the kiss was added in because  she reacted so nervously  you were so freaked out that i was like  well i gotta make her do it now  uh do you remember being 15 we do  and having our first kiss in front of a  crew of hundreds would have freaked us  out too  even though it all turned out okay in  the end the moment sparked an important  conversation about advocating for the  rights of young actors on set  millie bobby brown and finn wolfhard  have grown super close over the course  of filming stranger things  which makes for some amazing on-screen  chemistry just check out this adorable  scene of the two of them playing around  i never gave up on you i heard  you can't fake that kind of friendship  which is what makes the fact that their  very sweet scene in the grocery store  from season 3 was  actually all improv even better  poor mike is struggling to find the  words to tell elle that he wants to get  back together with her  and we all know how hard that can be i  just like i've never felt  like this you know with anyone before so  when finn started going off script and  trying to find a way to confess his love  for her  the directors absolutely loved it and  told him to keep going like like  old people say to each other sometimes  some actors will do just about anything  to stay in character  even when it terrifies their co-stars  just ask anyone who's ever worked with  jared leto  is he crazy well it turns out that dager  montgomery who plays the only human  being who has ever been intimidating in  a mullet  philly takes after leto in his own way  daker was so determined to stay in  character as his psychotic possessed by  evil forces character that he threw  caution to the wind  and almost broke his own skull during a  take i've done things max really  bad things in the harrowing sauna  sequence from season three  billy was only supposed to scream at the  kids from behind the sauna window  but instead he went ahead and smashed  his head against the thick glass so hard  that it actually  shattered luckily he walked away with no  lasting injuries  and no one can say the reactions he got  from the kids weren't totally authentic  max get away from the door what get away  from the door  the entire sauna episode was no easy  feat not for  anyone involved apparently it took four  days to shoot the emotionally wrought  sequence  and by the end of it everyone was  completely exhausted  no one more so than millie bobby brown  whose showdown against billy drained  both the character  and the actor physically and  psychologically  i was walking every single day director  sean levy said that  all of the exhaustion you see on screen  is completely real  and that the moment when eleven  collapses into mike's arms and start  sobbing  wasn't in the script at all but was just  the actress herself falling apart  and we don't blame her you can see finn  breaking character and looking over at  the director for guidance before  wrapping his arms around millie to  comfort her  she's such a dedicated actress that it's  easy to forget how young she is  and what a toll this kind of work must  take after so long  11 is me like 11 is just who i am now  even though he had tormented her and  everyone around her for the entire third  season  when it came to the final moments  between billy and eleven  millie bobby brown decided to show some  empathy for his incredibly tortured  character  right at the very end eleven sees into  billy's memories  and reminds him of a day at the beach  with his mother long before everything  went wrong in his life  turning him into a monster you told her  the wave was seven feet while it wasn't  in the script  she reaches up and touches his face  which when you think about it  is probably one of the only times that  billy has ever experienced real kindness  since his mother passed away  moving on to something a little less  tragic remember the hilarious breakfast  scene between nancy murray and jonathan  you know the morning after well it turns  out that one of the funniest parts of  that cringe-worthy brunch was entirely  made-up  brett gelman who plays murray is one of  the best comic actors out there  and when he saw an opportunity to make  the painful scene even more  uncomfortable  he had to take it right after asking a  few innuendo heavy questions about how  their night on the pull out couch was  gelman accidentally dropped a fork full  of eggs  instead of just picking it up and  continuing he instead said this  oops you can clearly see natalia dyer  doing her best not to burst out laughing  at the ad-lib  and we don't know if we could have been  that strong either  david harper's hopper try saying that  three times  is one of the highlights of the show  even if he can be  seriously grumpy sometimes but his  grumpiness really does come from a place  of love  and it only makes his character more  endearing when you say date  just so that we're crystal clear about  things yeah stop talking i  changed my mind while he has said that  he doesn't improvise a ton of lines  he adds in a lot of different behaviors  that are definitely not on the page  one example of this kind of thing goes  all the way back to season one  on the page it was really written as a  sweet caring scene  but instead harper decided that hopper  would try to get jonathan to toughen up  and approached it from a way  tougher place even going so far as to  punch him on the shoulder  you're crazy crazy  you wanna see real crazy back when she  was first getting to develop the  character of eleven  millie bobby brown decided that she  wanted to find a few moments where the  young girl could be a little bit funny  even if that wasn't in the script at all  one of her most iconic moments was  totally improv  that's right it's the eggo scene in the  script they had eleven go to the fridge  and pull out  one or maybe two boxes of waffles but  instead  millie had the idea to take just about  as many as she could carry  and honestly who can't relate to that  excuse me  a young lady holly wheeler nancy's  younger sister  has been on the show since the very  beginning and you might be surprised to  hear that she's actually played by two  twins  anison and tinsley price the price  sisters were  only two years old when they started  filming the show so they weren't given a  whole lot of lines  none in fact literally everything that  holly has ever said on screen has been  improv  and most of her reactions as well it's  okay ollie it's just a loud noise  it turns out that two-year-olds are  pretty priceless in their reactions  so if you turn a camera on them you're  bound to get something great  i'm gonna blow some daylight into that  thick skull of yours  no harper has had some great fights in  stranger things history  but his battle with gregory was one of  the best and apparently  all it said in the original script was  they fight  which isn't much to go off of but  working with their stunt coordinator  they had a great time coming up with the  epic showdown and based most of it off  of the indiana jones movie raiders of  the lost ark  they even got to throw some action hero  lines of their own into it  you wouldn't do that why's that  because you're a policeman after hearing  the story of how millie bobby brown  actually collapsed into finn's arms out  of exhaustion we have even more respect  for this dedicated cast  they really bring so much to each of  their characters especially when they go  off bug  and we cannot wait for season four how  about you  thanks for watching
 

